course: dictionary
lesson: 6951
title: Pal, friend or stranger?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pal is an informal word for a friend. «Double presents!» says her pal. The happy, sharing mood of the sentence tells you the two are close.
explain: Pal can also be said in an annoyed way to a stranger. «Listen, pal…» is not friendly, because the tone and the words around it show the speaker is cross. Always check the clues around the word.
explain: A pen pal is a special kind of pal. It means someone you write letters to, often in another country. Pupils have pen pals to practise their writing and learn about other places.
fact: Pal is an informal word for a friend, used in everyday talk and stories.
fact: «My old pal» and «best pals» show that two people are friends.
fact: A pen pal is someone you write letters to, often in another country.
fact: «Listen, pal…» can sound annoyed when said to a stranger.
fact: In Scotland, «ma pal» means my friend, and «wee» means small.
exercise: «Double presents!» says her pal. What is a pal here? | A teacher | A shop worker | *A friend | A driver
exercise: «Listen, pal…» is said to someone you do not know. What does the word show? | The speaker is happy to meet them | The speaker is a best friend | *The speaker is annoyed with a stranger | The speaker is giving a lesson
exercise: What is a pen pal? | A friend you only see at school | A pen with a friendly face | *Someone you write letters to, often in another country | A teacher who writes letters
test: Her pals say «Aw, he's pure cute». What does pure mean here? | Only just | Clean and spotless | *Really | Pale and white
test: «Mate, I'll stay pals, but I'm no believing anything you say till you stop.» What does stay pals suggest? | They will stop being friends | They will meet tomorrow | They are now strangers | *They will still be friends, though trust is hurt
exam: In Scotland, «ma pal» means what? | My brother | *My friend | My dog | My teacher
